{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>התרפית</b>, <b>הצל</b>, <b>כי</b> — [י-יב] three connected words." "<b>התרפית ביום צרה</b> — that comes upon your fellow and you did not rescue him." "<b>צר כחכה</b> — at the time of your distress. The meaning: rescue, if you withhold from those taken to death when their distress comes, and you say we did not know the time they were taken to death — does He not probe hearts to do His will, and He who guards your soul from death, He will understand and see that you did not wish to rescue them, and He will requite a man like you according to your deed, so that you will be in distress like him and find no rescuer."], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:24:29.092730708Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}